== Fault Recovery ==
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"I suspended the `audit-log-archiver` CronJob and submitted the mitigation. The submission was accepted. I'm not certain this CronJob was what degraded service.\n\n- **What I found:** All application pods were Running and every service had endpoints. The frontend's \"CheckAvailability failed\" errors were all timestamped 06:27:08, around startup, and none appeared afterward. Test requests through the frontend for search, recommendations and reservation all returned 200 quickly.\n- **The anomaly:** The only misbehaving workload was the `audit-log-archiver` CronJob. It runs every minute with `concurrencyPolicy: Allow`. Its `fluent-bit-sidecar` container never exits, so each job pod stayed at 1/2 NotReady and a new one piled up every minute.\n- **The fix:** I set `suspend: true` and `concurrencyPolicy: Forbid` on the CronJob, and deleted its two running jobs.\n- **Side effect:** The audit archive no longer runs. To bring it back, un-suspend the CronJob after fixing the sidecar so it exits when the archiver finishes."}}
